  "caption": "Quinn's tote bag holds everything, and by 3pm the whole arm feels heavy, with tingly little fingers and an achy neck.\n\nNerves (and sometimes blood vessels) pass through a tight space between the neck, first rib and collarbone. Overhead work, heavy bags, hiked-up shoulders and upper-chest breathing may all add pressure there.\n\nWhat often helps: lighten your bag or use both backpack straps, set up your desk and car so your shoulders can drop, practise relaxed lower breathing, and build shoulder strength with gentle nerve gliding. Progress is usually gradual.\n\nSudden arm swelling, colour change or a cold arm needs prompt medical care. Symptoms that keep building are worth assessing.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
